 "intro": {
  "title": "TUNING FORK FIELDS",
  "lines": [
   "Every row on this hill is a fork, and every fork has been tuned.",
   "What gets struck here is paid for somewhere else."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "Next: the Reliquary Road, where the Vael keep the people they have finished with.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [18, 68],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Terraces, and on every terrace a row of standing forks, brass and green, taller than a man. They are all humming. Not a sound I would put a word to."
  },
  {
   "id": "fork",
   "at": [24, 64],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A fork rings at a shot, answers its neighbours down the row, and everything asleep near them wakes. The arc lamp and a blow are heard from least far."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [30, 65],
   "radius": 2.5,
   "speaker": "FORK PLATE",
   "text": "A brass plate hammered onto the foot, in our letters: PELLEW, S. MATE. Somebody here had that courtesy. I count eight more plates in this row."
  },
  {
   "id": "tend",
   "at": [40, 52],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "They are tending the forks. Weeding round them, wiping them down, putting an ear to them. Nobody looks up. I would like to keep it that way."
  },
  {
   "id": "count",
   "at": [40, 46],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: a long number, a longer number, then one short note that rises like a question. Struck and owed, if I had to guess."
  },
  {
   "id": "tower",
   "at": [40, 25],
   "radius": 3.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A round tower on the top terrace with a bell inside it the size of a boat. Everything on this hill is tuned to that."
  },
  {
   "id": "lever",
   "at": [33, 16],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A lever on the bell stand. It works the gate in the north wall; the Keepers ring the bell and the gate answers."
  },
  {
   "id": "tune",
   "at": [0, 0],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The gate in the north wall opens. Down the hill, every fork in every field gives one low note, and stops."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [64, 66],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The east wall of this field rings hollow behind the last fork."
  }
 ],
 "objective": "Climb the hill: a stair at the end of each hall. The tower is on the plateau",
